                </row>
            </tabular>
        </statement>
    </exercise>

    <exercise workspace="3in">
        <statement>
            <p>
                The table below shows the amount of Strontium-90 (in mBq) in a simple random sample of baby teeth obtained from Pennsylvania and New York residents born after 1979. Use a 5% significance level to test the claim that Pennsylvania residents have a higher median amount of Strongtium-90 in their baby teeth than New York residents. 
            </p>
            <tabular>
                <row>
                    <cell>Pennsylvania</cell>
                        <cell>155</cell>
                        <cell>142</cell>
                        <cell>149</cell>
                        <cell>130</cell>
                        <cell>151</cell>
                        <cell>163</cell>
                        <cell>151</cell>
                        <cell>142</cell>
                        <cell>156</cell>
                        <cell>133</cell>
                        <cell>138</cell>
                        <cell>161</cell>
                </row>
                <row>
                    <cell>New York</cell>
                        <cell>133</cell>
                        <cell>140</cell>
                        <cell>142</cell>
                        <cell>131</cell>
                        <cell>134</cell>
                        <cell>129</cell>
                        <cell>128</cell>
                        <cell>140</cell>
                        <cell>140</cell>
                        <cell>140</cell>
                        <cell>137</cell>
                        <cell>143</cell>
                </row>
            </tabular>
        </statement>
    </exercise>

